[?2004hroot@e99295eb3257:/task# cat /task/input/lab_notes.md
[?2004l# Wet-lab notes: compound vs vehicle, primary cells

- Cells: primary cells from 12 unrelated donors (one culture per donor), passage 2.
- Treatment: compound at 1 uM or vehicle (0.1% DMSO) for 24 h; one condition per donor.
- RNA: column purification with on-column DNase; RIN >= 8.9 for all samples.
- Gene panel: the transcripts in `reference/` (targeted panel plus sex-chromosome control genes).
- Library prep: poly-A selection, unstranded. Two prep sessions because the first kit lot ran out: 2024-05-14 (6 libraries, kit lot A, operator 1) and 2024-06-04 (6 libraries, kit lot B, operator 2, different PCR cycler). The session of each library is in the sample sheet.
- Sequencing: all libraries pooled equimolar on one lane, 50-cycle single read. The core delivered adapter-trimmed reads; read names and base qualities were stripped to placeholders by their export tool.
[?2004hroot@e99295eb3257:/task# cat /task/input/previous_analysis/HANDOVER.md
[?2004l# Hand-over note: compound vs vehicle RNA-seq

Written on my last day. Sorry for the state of things.

## What is in this folder
- `scripts/01_quantify.sh` - salmon index and quantification of the 12 FASTQ files
- `scripts/02_merge_counts.py` - gene-level matrix from the salmon output
- `scripts/03_de.py` - DESeq2 model (pydeseq2), compound vs vehicle
- `gene_counts_merged.tsv` - gene-level matrix (output of 01 + 02)
- `de_draft.tsv` - draft differential-expression table (output of 03)
- `mail_top_responders.tsv` - the 40 genes I mailed to the wet lab on 2 July as "top responder genes"

## Notes
- The salmon output directories were on the scratch disk, which has been purged since. Only the
  merged matrix is left.
- The mailed list came from my first differential-expression run (smallest adjusted p-values first,
  sex-chromosome control genes taken out). The table of that run was overwritten; `de_draft.tsv` is
  from a later run.
- Samples were used as listed in the sample sheet.
- The wet lab has started to order qPCR primers for the mailed genes, so they need to know soon
  which of them hold up.
- All scripts take their paths as arguments, see the usage line at the top of each.
